# Chart and Data Visualization Patterns

## Chart Library
- **ECharts**: Primary charting library (NOT Recharts)
- **echarts-for-react**: React wrapper for ECharts
- **Chart Config**: [src/lib/chart-config.ts](mdc:src/lib/chart-config.ts) - Shared chart configurations

## Chart Components
- [src/components/charts/BarChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/BarChart.tsx) - Bar charts
- [src/components/charts/LineChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/LineChart.tsx) - Line charts
- [src/components/charts/VoteShareChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/VoteShareChart.tsx) - Vote share visualization
- [src/components/charts/ProgressChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/ProgressChart.tsx) - Progress indicators
- [src/components/charts/HorizontalBarChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/HorizontalBarChart.tsx) - Horizontal bars
- [src/components/charts/EChartsLineChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/EChartsLineChart.tsx) - ECharts line chart
- [src/components/charts/DemographicsChart.tsx](mdc:src/components/charts/DemographicsChart.tsx) - Demographic data

## Chart Usage Pattern
```typescript
import ReactECharts from 'echarts-for-react';

const MyChart = ({ data }) => {
  const option = {
    // ECharts configuration
    xAxis: { type: 'category', data: data.categories },
    yAxis: { type: 'value' },
    series: [{ data: data.values, type: 'bar' }],
  };

  return <ReactECharts option={option} style={{ height: '400px' }} />;
};
```

## Chart Configuration
- Use shared configurations from chart-config.ts
- Support dark mode with theme-aware colors
- Make charts responsive
- Include proper tooltips and legends

## Data Format
- Transform API data to chart format
- Handle empty data gracefully
- Support real-time data updates
- Cache chart data when appropriate

## Chart Styling
- Use consistent color schemes
- Support dark mode
- Make charts responsive
- Include proper spacing and padding

## Performance
- Memoize chart options
- Use React.memo for chart components
- Lazy load charts when possible
- Optimize large datasets

## Accessibility
- Include descriptive titles
- Provide data tables for screen readers
- Use proper color contrast
- Support keyboard navigation

## Common Chart Types
- Bar charts for comparisons
- Line charts for trends
- Pie charts for distributions
- Area charts for cumulative data
- Scatter plots for correlations

## Error Handling
- Handle missing data
- Display loading states
- Show error messages
- Provide fallback UI
